we get into that mindset that then keeps us stuck.

2071
01:30:03.690 --> 01:30:06.060
What we have to do is learn to embrace

2072
01:30:06.060 --> 01:30:08.100
the apprenticeship mindset,

2073
01:30:08.100 --> 01:30:10.280
and technology and the resources

2074
01:30:10.280 --> 01:30:12.280
are available to us in our fingertips.

2075
01:30:12.280 --> 01:30:13.970
We can have virtual mentors

2076
01:30:13.970 --> 01:30:18.300
and create our own apprenticeship instantly,

2077
01:30:18.300 --> 01:30:20.450
all we have to do, and this is the key,

2078
01:30:20.450 --> 01:30:22.750
this is how you discover your path passion.

2079
01:30:22.750 --> 01:30:24.520
Even if you don't know what your passion is,

2080
01:30:24.520 --> 01:30:26.980
here's how you discover your passion,

2081
01:30:26.980 --> 01:30:30.020
allow yourself to care more than normal

2082
01:30:30.020 --> 01:30:33.653
and more than necessary about an activity.

2083
01:30:34.690 --> 01:30:39.190
And then when you allow yourself to care more than normal,

2084
01:30:39.190 --> 01:30:41.730
about something and more than necessary,

2085
01:30:41.730 --> 01:30:43.700
you start to move out of the realm

2086
01:30:43.700 --> 01:30:45.710
of being your average self.

2087
01:30:45.710 --> 01:30:50.710
You start to step into that fanatical realm

2088
01:30:51.040 --> 01:30:55.210
of let me really explore and really chase this rabbit hole

2089
01:30:55.210 --> 01:30:56.863
to see how far it really goes,

2090
01:30:58.304 --> 01:31:03.070
all we have to begin doing is just caring about it more

2091
01:31:03.070 --> 01:31:05.813
than the average person,

2092
01:31:05.813 --> 01:31:07.010
and what that does is start to unfold.

2093
01:31:07.010 --> 01:31:10.490
You'll find out very quickly whether or not

2094
01:31:10.490 --> 01:31:14.150
something grabs your heart or resonates with you or not,

2095
01:31:14.150 --> 01:31:15.323
you'll find it.

2096
01:31:15.323 --> 01:31:16.800
And if it doesn't, cool, guess what?

2097
01:31:16.800 --> 01:31:18.490
You move on to something else.

2098
01:31:18.490 --> 01:31:20.654
And if that doesn't work, great,

2099
01:31:20.654 --> 01:31:21.969
you move on to something else.

2100
01:31:21.969 --> 01:31:24.950
The value in that discovery process is that,

2101
01:31:24.950 --> 01:31:26.560
again, God doesn't waste time in our lives,

2102
01:31:26.560 --> 01:31:28.330
whatever process we go through,

2103
01:31:28.330 --> 01:31:32.300
we will discover something that leads us to ultimately

2104
01:31:32.300 --> 01:31:34.150
what it is we really want,

2105
01:31:34.150 --> 01:31:37.440
but we've gotta be willing to move down that process,

2106
01:31:37.440 --> 01:31:39.950
we've gotta be willing to be an apprenticed.

2107
01:31:39.950 --> 01:31:42.433
And then I would also add to that,

2108
01:31:44.000 --> 01:31:45.150
many people say, in fact,

2109
01:31:45.150 --> 01:31:47.260
a guy that I was coaching said something

2110
01:31:47.260 --> 01:31:48.300
that was just authentic.

2111
01:31:48.300 --> 01:31:52.960
He asked this question in just very, very pure innocence.

2112
01:31:52.960 --> 01:31:54.366
He says, "Byron,

2113
01:31:54.366 --> 01:31:55.617
"what if you desire to do something

2114
01:31:55.617 --> 01:31:58.723
"that you really don't believe you can do?

2115
01:31:59.800 --> 01:32:00.633
"You don't have the confidence,

2116
01:32:00.633 --> 01:32:03.440
"you don't believe that you can actually do it."

2117
01:32:03.440 --> 01:32:05.333
And it was a great question.

2118
01:32:06.605 --> 01:32:09.110
And the short answer is this,

2119
01:32:09.110 --> 01:32:12.660
you learn how to, number one,

2120
01:32:12.660 --> 01:32:16.180
discount your own voice in the process.

2121
01:32:16.180 --> 01:32:17.790
Okay, that's a step one

2122
01:32:17.790 --> 01:32:20.680
because you really don't have the authority

2123
01:32:20.680 --> 01:32:21.910
or the credibility-

2124
01:32:21.910 --> 01:32:23.640
To make that judgment call.
To make that judgment

2125
01:32:23.640 --> 01:32:26.450
because you failed at it so far, you haven't done it.

2126
01:32:26.450 --> 01:32:28.800
So you can't make that judgment.

2127
01:32:28.800 --> 01:32:32.850
So logically, if you wanted to know something

2128
01:32:32.850 --> 01:32:35.920
about financial investing and you had an opportunity

2129
01:32:35.920 --> 01:32:37.450
to learn under Warren Buffet

2130
01:32:37.450 --> 01:32:39.300
or learn under someone who's tried really hard,

2131
01:32:39.300 --> 01:32:40.650
but hasn't gotten the results you want.

2132
01:32:40.650 --> 01:32:42.170
Who would you choose?

2133
01:32:42.170 --> 01:32:43.260
Warren Buffet, right.

2134
01:32:43.260 --> 01:32:44.240
You would wanna do that.

2135
01:32:44.240 --> 01:32:46.990
So in this case, in this scenario,

2136
01:32:46.990 --> 01:32:48.360
when you really realize

2137
01:32:48.360 --> 01:32:49.717
that I don't know how to do something,

2138
01:32:49.717 --> 01:32:51.920
and I don't really think I can,

2139
01:32:51.920 --> 01:32:53.260
you've gotta recognize in that moment

2140
01:32:53.260 --> 01:32:55.350
that you're not the Warren Buffet in the situation,

2141
01:32:55.350 --> 01:32:57.370
you are the other person.

2142
01:32:57.370 --> 01:32:59.730
You're not in a place to even objectively judge

2143
01:32:59.730 --> 01:33:01.240
whether you can or cannot do that.

2144
01:33:01.240 --> 01:33:02.600
Exactly, exactly.

2145
01:33:02.600 --> 01:33:05.670
So why be unfair to yourself in that?

2146
01:33:05.670 --> 01:33:08.420
And the second step is, so once you acknowledge that,

2147
01:33:08.420 --> 01:33:09.253
you know what?

2148
01:33:09.253 --> 01:33:11.360
I've gotta discount my own judgment,

2149
01:33:11.360 --> 01:33:13.810
my own belief in this situation,

2150
01:33:13.810 --> 01:33:16.443
the second step then is to submit yourself,

2151
01:33:17.880 --> 01:33:20.520
become obedient to a proven process.

2152
01:33:20.520 --> 01:33:22.440
So now you have to now

2153
01:33:24.210 --> 01:33:29.210
give your trust and your faith over to a proven process.

2154
01:33:29.560 --> 01:33:32.360
So that's when you seek out, who's doing this?

2155
01:33:32.360 --> 01:33:34.498
Who's gotten the results that you need to get?

2156
01:33:34.498 --> 01:33:35.750
If you think, well, I'm not musically inclined,

2157
01:33:35.750 --> 01:33:36.760
I've no musical talent.

2158
01:33:36.760 --> 01:33:39.570
I'll never be able to play the piano or whatever

2159
01:33:39.570 --> 01:33:42.150
and then saying, well, I'm gonna go to this teacher.

2160
01:33:42.150 --> 01:33:43.840
And I will apprentice to this person

2161
01:33:43.840 --> 01:33:45.990
who has taught many people how to play the piano.

2162
01:33:45.990 --> 01:33:50.190
It's a proven procedure and process that I can undertake.

2163
01:33:50.190 --> 01:33:53.370
Yeah, and we know this as athletes,

2164
01:33:53.370 --> 01:33:56.137
there comes a point where we have to buy

2165
01:33:56.137 --> 01:33:58.110
into the culture and the methodology

2166
01:33:58.110 --> 01:33:59.690
of the program we're in.

2167
01:33:59.690 --> 01:34:04.010
If we don't buy into how the coach is preparing us,

2168
01:34:04.010 --> 01:34:06.210
then we'll second guess our preparation.

2169
01:34:06.210 --> 01:34:08.740
And then we'll lose all confidence in our ability.

2170
01:34:08.740 --> 01:34:09.630
There comes a point

2171
01:34:09.630 --> 01:34:12.670
where you have to give your trust over to the process.

2172
01:34:12.670 --> 01:34:14.770
You have to fall in love with the process.

2173
01:34:14.770 --> 01:34:16.670
You have to give your heart to the process.

2174
01:34:16.670 --> 01:34:18.220
Again, you've gotta care more than normal

2175
01:34:18.220 --> 01:34:19.730
and more than necessary.

2176
01:34:19.730 --> 01:34:21.550
And then what takes place

2177
01:34:21.550 --> 01:34:24.920
is you suspend your disbelief long enough

2178
01:34:24.920 --> 01:34:27.470
that you then invite new experiences

2179
01:34:27.470 --> 01:34:29.490
that give you better results

2180
01:34:29.490 --> 01:34:33.820
from which you can then base better and stronger beliefs on.

2181
01:34:33.820 --> 01:34:37.570
So your beliefs ultimately will catch up to your experience,

2182
01:34:37.570 --> 01:34:39.100
and that's where confidence comes from.

2183
01:34:39.100 --> 01:34:41.410
And it all goes back to trying to propel

2184
01:34:41.410 --> 01:34:44.920
some of this moment that we were talking about earlier.

2185
01:34:44.920 --> 01:34:48.370
And so I'm not a advocate of just pump yourself up

2186
01:34:48.370 --> 01:34:52.334
and muster off enough confidence to do something.

2187
01:34:52.334 --> 01:34:53.994
Well, it brings false.

2188
01:34:53.994 --> 01:34:57.740
It's not backed up by anything.

2189
01:34:57.740 --> 01:34:58.763
It's pretending.

2190
01:35:00.210 --> 01:35:02.883
Allow yourself to embrace,

2191
01:35:04.110 --> 01:35:05.542
it's like this,

2192
01:35:05.542 --> 01:35:06.410
so when I speak to athletes

2193
01:35:06.410 --> 01:35:08.853
and I go out and talk, I say,

2194
01:35:09.770 --> 01:35:11.520
at times you will not be confident.

2195
01:35:12.590 --> 01:35:13.960
Recognize that, embrace it.

2196
01:35:13.960 --> 01:35:16.480
Don't be surprised if, and when it happens,

2197
01:35:16.480 --> 01:35:18.070
confidence has very little to do

2198
01:35:18.070 --> 01:35:21.880
with your capability of actually doing it, making it happen.

2199
01:35:21.880 --> 01:35:25.560
In that moment, don't worry about not being confident.

2200
01:35:25.560 --> 01:35:28.070
Allow yourself to be curious.

2201
01:35:28.070 --> 01:35:29.570
We can all be curious.

2202
01:35:29.570 --> 01:35:32.630
We can all allow ourselves to go into a moment

2203
01:35:32.630 --> 01:35:35.380
into a situation where we don't know the answer,

2204
01:35:35.380 --> 01:35:37.950
we acknowledge we don't know the answer,

2205
01:35:37.950 --> 01:35:42.060
but we all can embrace that and be very curious.

2206
01:35:42.060 --> 01:35:44.673
And when we're curious, it's just like a kid.

2207
01:35:44.673 --> 01:35:45.610
When you're curious about something,

2208
01:35:45.610 --> 01:35:47.650
you put on the hat of a professor,

2209
01:35:47.650 --> 01:35:52.240
your awareness, and in all of your energy,

2210
01:35:52.240 --> 01:35:56.210
your brain power starts to become acutely aware

2211
01:35:56.210 --> 01:36:01.210
of scenarios, of patterns, of little answers,

2212
01:36:01.890 --> 01:36:05.080
all these things start to now come at you

2213
01:36:05.080 --> 01:36:08.069
when you decide to be curious,

2214
01:36:08.069 --> 01:36:11.160
you invite enough room to create experiences

2215
01:36:11.160 --> 01:36:13.883
that then you can start to stack up,

2216
01:36:13.883 --> 01:36:14.810
that will become your confidence.

2217
01:36:14.810 --> 01:36:16.827
So you don't have to be confident.

2218
01:36:16.827 --> 01:36:18.020
You don't have to believe you can do something

2219
01:36:18.020 --> 01:36:19.050
in order to do it,

2220
01:36:19.050 --> 01:36:21.680
just allow yourself to be curious enough

2221
01:36:21.680 --> 01:36:26.680
to move through that moment and that period of ambiguity,

2222
01:36:27.140 --> 01:36:29.217
and then allow the small incremental results

2223
01:36:29.217 --> 01:36:33.400
you get to dictate your mid-course corrections

2224
01:36:33.400 --> 01:36:35.610
so that ultimately you will cross the finish line.

2225
01:36:35.610 --> 01:36:37.220
Right, and that confidence

2226
01:36:37.220 --> 01:36:38.480
will come as a result of that.

2227
01:36:38.480 --> 01:36:40.400
It's sort of acting as if, it's like,

2228
01:36:40.400 --> 01:36:41.810
I don't believe this is gonna work,

2229
01:36:41.810 --> 01:36:44.440
but I'm gonna show up and do it anyway.

2230
01:36:44.440 --> 01:36:48.080
And then over time this sort of objective feedback

2231
01:36:48.080 --> 01:36:51.520
becomes undeniable that, oh, actually I can do this,

2232
01:36:51.520 --> 01:36:53.433
or I proved myself wrong.

2233
01:36:54.339 --> 01:36:55.172
And I always talk about this too,

2234
01:36:55.172 --> 01:36:57.600
it's sort of understanding that (clears throat)

2235
01:36:57.600 --> 01:36:59.623
your mind is not always your friend.

2236
01:37:00.530 --> 01:37:03.030
And when it's firing signals off saying you can't,

2237
01:37:03.946 --> 01:37:06.000
or I stink or I'll never be good or whatever,

2238
01:37:06.000 --> 01:37:08.790
those are just messages, and that you have a choice,

2239
01:37:08.790 --> 01:37:12.800
your higher self has a choice to give those credence

2240
01:37:12.800 --> 01:37:15.320
or to dismiss them and say,

2241
01:37:15.320 --> 01:37:16.900
hey, that's interesting that my brain

2242
01:37:16.900 --> 01:37:19.441
is trying to tell me that I can't do that.

2243
01:37:19.441 --> 01:37:21.120
But I'm just gonna shrug that off

2244
01:37:21.120 --> 01:37:23.980
and not pay attention to that because I know better,

2245
01:37:23.980 --> 01:37:28.980
or I choose to believe otherwise or act differently.

2246
01:37:30.544 --> 01:37:32.350
Yeah, I call that our inner-child.

2247
01:37:32.350 --> 01:37:34.550
Our inner-child will start acting up

2248
01:37:36.158 --> 01:37:37.210
and be rebellious.

2249
01:37:37.210 --> 01:37:40.955
But as the adult in the situation who has-

2250
01:37:40.955 --> 01:37:42.150
You have smack 'em down. (laughs)

2251
01:37:42.150 --> 01:37:43.830
You say, well, no, I'll demonstrate it.

2252
01:37:43.830 --> 01:37:46.710
I'll show you, take my hand, and I will lead the way,

2253
01:37:46.710 --> 01:37:48.870
in those moments when our defeated self

2254
01:37:48.870 --> 01:37:51.470
or when our average self want to take the lead in our life.

2255
01:37:51.470 --> 01:37:55.777
No, that's when our epic self has to say,

2256
01:37:55.777 --> 01:37:56.630
you know what?

2257
01:37:56.630 --> 01:37:59.140
I'm going to lead the way.

2258
01:37:59.140 --> 01:38:02.860
And we allow ourselves enough room to fail,

2259
01:38:02.860 --> 01:38:05.260
embrace that, because we know that, again,

2260
01:38:05.260 --> 01:38:07.363
that's the whole idea of iteration.

2261
01:38:08.373 --> 01:38:12.580
We recognize that, you know, my failure in 1996,

2262
01:38:12.580 --> 01:38:14.470
wasn't the end of my life,

2263
01:38:14.470 --> 01:38:18.310
but I was able to ultimately use that failure

2264
01:38:18.310 --> 01:38:22.220
to set up future success in different areas of my life.

2265
01:38:22.220 --> 01:38:26.240
Likewise, that's the attitude and the inner-culture

2266
01:38:26.240 --> 01:38:30.090
we have to embrace in order to really do things

2267
01:38:30.090 --> 01:38:31.690
that are meaningful in our life.

2268
01:38:32.762 --> 01:38:36.000
And I know I'm throwing a lot or going off on tangents here,

2269
01:38:36.000 --> 01:38:39.010
but it's for the same reason why I'm not

2270
01:38:39.010 --> 01:38:41.210
an advocate of setting goals,

2271
01:38:41.210 --> 01:38:44.586
the way we've always been taught in school.

2272
01:38:44.586 --> 01:38:47.960
I'm not an enemy to setting goals,

2273
01:38:47.960 --> 01:38:51.460
but I think we limit ourselves a lot

2274
01:38:51.460 --> 01:38:55.910
when we get trapped in the need to set goals.

2275
01:38:55.910 --> 01:38:58.430
What I do believe in is not setting goals

2276
01:38:58.430 --> 01:39:01.800
is not a license to not just do anything in life.

2277
01:39:01.800 --> 01:39:03.270
I'm not talking about that.

2278
01:39:03.270 --> 01:39:06.923
I'm talking about actually learning how to engage vision.

2279
01:39:08.072 --> 01:39:11.253
So learning to stop setting goals and start engaging vision.

2280
01:39:13.012 --> 01:39:15.603
What that means is learning how to own a process

2281
01:39:17.760 --> 01:39:19.573
and a plan in our life.

2282
01:39:20.570 --> 01:39:22.630
Many of us are afraid to make a choice,

2283
01:39:22.630 --> 01:39:24.740
make a decision because we're afraid

2284
01:39:24.740 --> 01:39:26.979
that decision will be wrong.

2285
01:39:26.979 --> 01:39:28.890
So we settle into this idea

2286
01:39:28.890 --> 01:39:31.510
that I don't know what my passion is.

2287
01:39:31.510 --> 01:39:33.428
What we're really saying is,

2288
01:39:33.428 --> 01:39:35.990
is I'm not willing to make a decision to draw a line

2289
01:39:35.990 --> 01:39:37.610
a definite line.
I think that's very true.

2290
01:39:37.610 --> 01:39:38.700
That's interesting.

2291
01:39:38.700 --> 01:39:41.290
And go with this good, bad or ugly,

2292
01:39:41.290 --> 01:39:43.320
but it's only when we decide

2293
01:39:43.320 --> 01:39:45.230
to make that definitive decision,

2294
01:39:45.230 --> 01:39:48.330
will we find out and we'll find out quickly

2295
01:39:48.330 --> 01:39:51.020
whether or not it was the right or wrong decision,

2296
01:39:51.020 --> 01:39:54.440
but if it turns out to be the wrong decision, that's okay.

2297
01:39:54.440 --> 01:39:55.850
Right, to give yourself permission

2298
01:39:55.850 --> 01:39:57.200
to make the wrong decision.

2299
01:39:58.060 --> 01:40:01.650
I think that goals are they have their place

2300
01:40:01.650 --> 01:40:04.590
in the sense that they create that structure

2301
01:40:04.590 --> 01:40:06.250
for people who operate well

2302
01:40:06.250 --> 01:40:09.880
within that kind of a paradigm like myself.

2303
01:40:09.880 --> 01:40:11.818
But I think you're correct,

2304
01:40:11.818 --> 01:40:13.418
and that what happens with goals

2305
01:40:14.668 --> 01:40:18.230
is that not only are they limiting

2306
01:40:18.230 --> 01:40:19.740
because you're putting a cap on it

2307
01:40:19.740 --> 01:40:23.810
and are you the best objective decision-maker to decide

2308
01:40:23.810 --> 01:40:27.233
what you're capable or not capable of, probably not.

2309
01:40:28.100 --> 01:40:32.130
And secondarily, they tend to be very destination oriented

2310
01:40:33.183 --> 01:40:34.583
instead of journey oriented,

2311
01:40:35.690 --> 01:40:38.870
so it's sort of all about the obvious example

2312
01:40:38.870 --> 01:40:40.180
is always the weight loss example.

2313
01:40:40.180 --> 01:40:41.350
Like I wanna lose 10 pounds

2314
01:40:41.350 --> 01:40:43.400
or I wanna lose 50 pounds,

2315
01:40:43.400 --> 01:40:45.440
and it's all about getting to that day

2316
01:40:45.440 --> 01:40:48.220
or crossing the finish line at that marathon

2317
01:40:48.220 --> 01:40:49.293
or whatever it is.

2318
01:40:50.379 --> 01:40:52.190
But then it's sort of the questions never asked

2319
01:40:52.190 --> 01:40:54.030
like, well now what?

2320
01:40:54.030 --> 01:40:54.863
You get there

2321
01:40:54.863 --> 01:40:58.893
and then you have the sort of what am I supposed to do now?

2322
01:40:58.893 --> 01:41:01.410
And then the kind of weird emotions that swirl around,

2323
01:41:01.410 --> 01:41:02.440
what happens next?

2324
01:41:02.440 --> 01:41:05.510
Because it was all about getting to that endpoint,

2325
01:41:05.510 --> 01:41:09.080
as opposed to being actively engaged in the moment

2326
01:41:09.080 --> 01:41:11.130
and in the destination and in the journey.

2327
01:41:11.130 --> 01:41:13.910
And even you hear it all the time,

2328
01:41:13.910 --> 01:41:15.300
people that achieve these goals,

2329
01:41:15.300 --> 01:41:17.440
whether it's an Olympic gold medal or whatever it is,

2330
01:41:17.440 --> 01:41:18.890
they'll always tell you,

2331
01:41:18.890 --> 01:41:23.350
well, thinking back on everything it took for me

2332
01:41:23.350 --> 01:41:25.910
to get there is where the best memories

2333
01:41:25.910 --> 01:41:29.310
are and where I really can engage the joy

2334
01:41:29.310 --> 01:41:31.770
was in that process and in the journey.

2335
01:41:31.770 --> 01:41:34.110
Yeah, and while I definitely believe

2336
01:41:35.150 --> 01:41:36.810
that the magic and the beauty

2337
01:41:36.810 --> 01:41:39.470
and the nectar is in the journey,

2338
01:41:39.470 --> 01:41:43.710
like you, I am a results guy, I like to see results,

2339
01:41:43.710 --> 01:41:48.710
but I also think that let's live a life that's prolific

2340
01:41:50.120 --> 01:41:53.320
as opposed to goal-oriented.

2341
01:41:53.320 --> 01:41:58.160
And what I mean by that is being prolific is establishing

2342
01:41:58.160 --> 01:42:02.010
a rhythm of life where we're accomplishing stuff,

2343
01:42:02.010 --> 01:42:05.890
meaningful stuff, stuff that matters on a regular basis.

2344
01:42:05.890 --> 01:42:10.160
When we think of Steven Spielberg or Stephen King,

2345
01:42:10.160 --> 01:42:11.590
we think these guys are prolific.

2346
01:42:11.590 --> 01:42:14.550
They keep coming out with great stuff over and over again,

2347
01:42:14.550 --> 01:42:16.920
for them, it's not about the goal,

2348
01:42:16.920 --> 01:42:21.410
for them, their work is just a snapshot

2349
01:42:21.410 --> 01:42:24.533
of their expression of their existence.

2350
01:42:25.590 --> 01:42:27.350
And before they finish one thing,

2351
01:42:27.350 --> 01:42:29.023
they're off to doing another,

2352
01:42:30.240 --> 01:42:33.700
and so it's that perpetual journey

2353
01:42:33.700 --> 01:42:36.113
that produces results is what I'm after.

2354
01:42:37.123 --> 01:42:39.175
That's living prolifically.

2355
01:42:39.175 --> 01:42:40.203
That that's what we want.

2356
01:42:41.195 --> 01:42:44.500
And guys will tell you, people will tell you, again,

2357
01:42:44.500 --> 01:42:47.440
after a big event, after the Super Bowl,

2358
01:42:47.440 --> 01:42:51.430
why is it that we hear story and story after story

2359
01:42:51.430 --> 01:42:53.590
of people doing something great?

2360
01:42:53.590 --> 01:42:56.780
And then immediately short time afterward,

2361
01:42:56.780 --> 01:42:58.802
they blow their brains out,

2362
01:42:58.802 --> 01:43:01.670
or they go off on the deep end or something.

2363
01:43:01.670 --> 01:43:02.970
And we're like, how did that happen?

2364
01:43:02.970 --> 01:43:05.990
It's because partly they got themselves

2365
01:43:05.990 --> 01:43:09.040
so wrapped up in defining who they were in that moment,

2366
01:43:09.040 --> 01:43:10.313
when the moment was gone,

2367
01:43:11.991 --> 01:43:15.150
if they didn't immediately have another hill to conquer,

2368
01:43:15.150 --> 01:43:16.610
they were lost.

2369
01:43:16.610 --> 01:43:20.410
Well, I say, let's not limit ourselves by that.

2370
01:43:20.410 --> 01:43:22.540
Let's have definite checkpoints.

2371
01:43:22.540 --> 01:43:25.363
Let's have moments where we can celebrate victory,

2372
01:43:26.261 --> 01:43:27.330
I'm totally into that.

2373
01:43:27.330 --> 01:43:29.590
But instead, let's create a lifestyle

2374
01:43:29.590 --> 01:43:33.640
and a culture within ourselves where we're producing

2375
01:43:33.640 --> 01:43:36.050
these things on a regular basis.

2376
01:43:36.050 --> 01:43:39.120
It's basically, just a constant manifestation

2377
01:43:39.120 --> 01:43:40.440
of who you are.

2378
01:43:40.440 --> 01:43:43.080
So as opposed to, yeah, I'm gonna win the Super Bowl,

2379
01:43:43.080 --> 01:43:45.380
or if your Spielberg it's just, this is what I do,

2380
01:43:45.380 --> 01:43:47.750
I'm doing it all the time, I'm onto the next thing.

2381
01:43:47.750 --> 01:43:50.130
And you're not overly attached

2382
01:43:50.130 --> 01:43:52.170
to the result of any one thing,

2383
01:43:52.170 --> 01:43:53.860
because that's not your focus,

2384
01:43:53.860 --> 01:43:58.140
your focus isn't crossing the finish line at the marathon

2385
01:43:58.140 --> 01:44:00.090
or what the scale says that day.

2386
01:44:00.090 --> 01:44:02.150
It's just, this is what I do now.

2387
01:44:02.150 --> 01:44:05.530
This is who I am, and I'm constantly expressing it.

2388
01:44:05.530 --> 01:44:08.340
It's a completely different perspective on the whole thing,

2389
01:44:08.340 --> 01:44:11.730
but yeah, that's very interesting.

2390
01:44:11.730 --> 01:44:13.410
Very good, yeah.

2391
01:44:13.410 --> 01:44:14.330
Cool.

2392
01:44:14.330 --> 01:44:15.980
Live prolifically.

2393
01:44:15.980 --> 01:44:17.853
Yeah, let's live a pro-
Live your epic life.

2394
01:44:17.853 --> 01:44:19.240
Live our epic life.

2395
01:44:19.240 --> 01:44:20.220
And here's the thing,

2396
01:44:20.220 --> 01:44:21.730
the reason why I say epic,

2397
01:44:21.730 --> 01:44:25.360
I know for some, that's kinda over-the-top,

2398
01:44:25.360 --> 01:44:26.563
live your epic life,

2399
01:44:27.540 --> 01:44:30.740
that's birthed out of the, again,

2400
01:44:30.740 --> 01:44:33.903
the conviction that we all have a story to tell in our life,

2401
01:44:35.279 --> 01:44:37.900
and every epic tale, whether we read it or in a book

2402
01:44:37.900 --> 01:44:40.933
or watch it in a movie has three main elements.

2403
01:44:42.100 --> 01:44:45.070
You have a flawed main character

2404
01:44:45.070 --> 01:44:48.120
who decides to embark on some type of ambition,

2405
01:44:48.120 --> 01:44:50.650
who ultimately must come up against an antagonist

2406
01:44:50.650 --> 01:44:53.730
or conflict in order to do so.

2407
01:44:53.730 --> 01:44:58.730
And it's in that process that the person's story plays out

2408
01:44:58.750 --> 01:45:03.440
that a transformation has to happen that ultimately allows

2409
01:45:03.440 --> 01:45:08.050
them to position themselves, to actually accomplishing

2410
01:45:08.050 --> 01:45:10.713
what it was that they once thought was impossible.

2411
01:45:12.250 --> 01:45:15.470
And what I believe is what makes for a great and epic story

2412
01:45:15.470 --> 01:45:16.963
also makes for an epic life.

2413
01:45:18.408 --> 01:45:19.663
Well, we all have that story,

2414
01:45:21.152 --> 01:45:23.520
it's this Joseph Campbell, "Hero's Journey,"

2415
01:45:23.520 --> 01:45:28.300
and it's incumbent upon all of us to be the hero

2416
01:45:28.300 --> 01:45:29.410
in our own movie.

2417
01:45:29.410 --> 01:45:30.243
You know what I mean?

2418
01:45:30.243 --> 01:45:31.770
Stop being an extra,

2419
01:45:31.770 --> 01:45:35.937
or a supporting actor in your own biopic.

2420
01:45:35.937 --> 01:45:38.960
Well said, yeah, exactly.

2421
01:45:38.960 --> 01:45:41.010
And we all have that power within us.

2422
01:45:41.010 --> 01:45:44.330
We all have that power and it does require a decision.

2423
01:45:44.330 --> 01:45:46.040
And it doesn't mean that it's easy

2424
01:45:47.165 --> 01:45:47.998
and it's not about buying a book

2425
01:45:47.998 --> 01:45:49.950
that's gonna give you the three steps

2426
01:45:49.950 --> 01:45:51.640
where you're not gonna have to do anything

2427
01:45:51.640 --> 01:45:52.750
and your life's gonna change

2428
01:45:52.750 --> 01:45:55.337
and you're gonna lose weight and all that kind of stuff.

2429
01:45:55.337 --> 01:45:57.370
You have to take personal responsibility for it.

2430
01:45:57.370 --> 01:46:00.130
But if you're willing to do the work and take direction

2431
01:46:00.130 --> 01:46:03.400
and engage in this apprenticeship,

2432
01:46:03.400 --> 01:46:07.670
which is sort of a lost art form in which we all used

2433
01:46:07.670 --> 01:46:11.063
to kind of grow up within the construct

2434
01:46:11.063 --> 01:46:11.896
of that's kind of gone away.

2435
01:46:11.896 --> 01:46:15.890
But I think because technology is becoming so predominant

2436
01:46:15.890 --> 01:46:18.430
as a part of our economy and so specific

2437
01:46:18.430 --> 01:46:20.560
that's really coming back, you know what I mean?

2438
01:46:20.560 --> 01:46:22.410
If you wanna be a film editor,

2439
01:46:22.410 --> 01:46:25.270
you have to apprentice with a film editor,

2440
01:46:25.270 --> 01:46:27.060
you can go to school and learn the software program,

2441
01:46:27.060 --> 01:46:30.110
but I think that you're seeing a resurgence of that.

2442
01:46:30.110 --> 01:46:32.283
And I think that that's a good thing.

2443
01:46:33.505 --> 01:46:35.630
It's like when I went and worked in a law firm.

2444
01:46:35.630 --> 01:46:38.310
Yeah, I had partners and senior associates

2445
01:46:38.310 --> 01:46:42.490
that I reported to, but it wasn't an apprenticeship,

2446
01:46:42.490 --> 01:46:44.410
there wasn't like one guy who said,

2447
01:46:44.410 --> 01:46:46.000
I'm gonna teach you how to do this

2448
01:46:46.000 --> 01:46:49.000
and you're gonna follow me around and do everything I do.

2449
01:46:49.000 --> 01:46:49.833
You know what I mean?

2450
01:46:49.833 --> 01:46:51.610
And I think that we could all benefit

2451
01:46:51.610 --> 01:46:53.450
from having more of that in our lives.

2452
01:46:53.450 --> 01:46:56.670
And we could all benefit from having a support system,

2453
01:47:00.898 --> 01:47:02.480
a strong mother who believed in you

2454
01:47:02.480 --> 01:47:04.800
and a Jeff Armstrong at the YMCA,

2455
01:47:04.800 --> 01:47:07.240
who went the extra mile to look out for you

2456
01:47:07.240 --> 01:47:08.870
because he believed in you.

2457
01:47:08.870 --> 01:47:12.310
And so I think we all need to look at ourselves

2458
01:47:12.310 --> 01:47:14.560
and at our own lives and say,

2459
01:47:14.560 --> 01:47:16.826
who is that person for us?

2460
01:47:16.826 --> 01:47:18.613
And who can I be that person for?

2461
01:47:19.530 --> 01:47:21.080
You just said something, man,

2462
01:47:22.085 --> 01:47:24.083
that's I think, magic, powerful.

2463
01:47:25.090 --> 01:47:28.600
There are situations and people out there right now who,

2464
01:47:28.600 --> 01:47:30.090
when they honestly look at their life,

2465
01:47:30.090 --> 01:47:31.280
they don't have that person.

2466
01:47:31.280 --> 01:47:33.790
They don't have a mom who's totally sold out

2467
01:47:33.790 --> 01:47:34.850
to investing in them.

2468
01:47:34.850 --> 01:47:38.683
They don't have that person who was a champion for them,

2469
01:47:39.650 --> 01:47:42.660
if and when they didn't believe in themselves.

2470
01:47:42.660 --> 01:47:45.847
Yeah, they are, but here's the key.

2471
01:47:45.847 --> 01:47:49.410
And I go back to, you jarred this in my mind,

2472
01:47:49.410 --> 01:47:52.006
my eighth-grade teacher always said

2473
01:47:52.006 --> 01:47:53.840
the fastest way to master or learn anything

2474
01:47:53.840 --> 01:47:57.040
is to turn around and immediately teach it to someone else.

2475
01:47:57.040 --> 01:48:02.040
Well, you can reverse engineer the whole apprentice process,

2476
01:48:02.430 --> 01:48:05.586
where all, again, you just decide that,

2477
01:48:05.586 --> 01:48:06.480
you know what?

2478
01:48:06.480 --> 01:48:10.680
I am going to teach or invest in someone else

2479
01:48:10.680 --> 01:48:13.370
and show them, demonstrate to them

2480
01:48:13.370 --> 01:48:15.460
how to get results in this area of your life.

2481
01:48:15.460 --> 01:48:18.050
And if you just do that, if you just even start there,

2482
01:48:18.050 --> 01:48:21.160
have the courage to start there, all of a sudden,

2483
01:48:21.160 --> 01:48:24.210
you will start out of the woodwork,

2484
01:48:24.210 --> 01:48:26.490
resources and relationships

2485
01:48:26.490 --> 01:48:28.730
and things you used to take for granted

2486
01:48:28.730 --> 01:48:30.370
that you look at at a different way,

2487
01:48:30.370 --> 01:48:31.940
will then become your teacher,

2488
01:48:31.940 --> 01:48:36.940
that they will become your source of content and information

2489
01:48:37.480 --> 01:48:40.310
that now starts to funnel through you.

2490
01:48:40.310 --> 01:48:43.840
And in the process of you just inviting someone else

2491
01:48:43.840 --> 01:48:45.800
along the process with you,

2492
01:48:45.800 --> 01:48:48.600
you begin to practice the very thing

2493
01:48:48.600 --> 01:48:50.570
you once thought you couldn't do.

2494
01:48:50.570 --> 01:48:52.740
So really learning,

2495
01:48:52.740 --> 01:48:54.300
and if you don't have anybody

2496
01:48:54.300 --> 01:48:56.630
that you can think of right off the top of your mind,

2497
01:48:56.630 --> 01:49:00.170
that's your champion and all that,

2498
01:49:00.170 --> 01:49:05.170
that's no excuse to not immediately turn around

2499
01:49:05.230 --> 01:49:08.350
and invest yourself, put yourself on the line,

2500
01:49:08.350 --> 01:49:10.150
call yourself to the carpet and say, you know what?

2501
01:49:10.150 --> 01:49:12.290
I don't quite know how to do this yet,

2502
01:49:12.290 --> 01:49:13.990
but I am committed to showing

2503
01:49:13.990 --> 01:49:17.200
and demonstrating someone else the best approach to do it.

2504
01:49:17.200 --> 01:49:20.850
And just putting yourself in that position immediately,

2505
01:49:20.850 --> 01:49:25.850
all of a sudden, you now become this honing device

2506
01:49:26.940 --> 01:49:30.190
where all these resources and all of the information

2507
01:49:30.190 --> 01:49:33.655
you need will start to come together for you,

2508
01:49:33.655 --> 01:49:35.650
and in the process of you sharing, you giving yourself,

2509
01:49:35.650 --> 01:49:37.720
you pouring yourself into someone else,

2510
01:49:37.720 --> 01:49:38.890
you benefit in the process.

2511
01:49:38.890 --> 01:49:40.560
Yeah, absolutely.

2512
01:49:40.560 --> 01:49:42.480
That's something I learned a long time ago

2513
01:49:42.480 --> 01:49:46.063
and is a key cornerstone in recovery,

2514
01:49:48.300 --> 01:49:52.700
essentially that, if you're feeling stuck or you're unhappy,

2515
01:49:52.700 --> 01:49:55.900
or you get wrapped up in your story of why your life

2516
01:49:55.900 --> 01:49:57.970
isn't the way you want it to be?

2517
01:49:57.970 --> 01:49:59.603
Or you're getting all sort of,

2518
01:50:02.390 --> 01:50:03.890
what's the word for it?

2519
01:50:03.890 --> 01:50:05.340
Just sort of self-defeating

2520
01:50:05.340 --> 01:50:08.070
and running these patterns in your brain,

2521
01:50:08.070 --> 01:50:09.860
you can't think your way out of that,

2522
01:50:09.860 --> 01:50:12.295
you've gotta act your way out of it.

2523
01:50:12.295 --> 01:50:13.650
And the best way to act your way out of it

2524
01:50:13.650 --> 01:50:16.730
is to reach out to somebody and be of service to them.

2525
01:50:16.730 --> 01:50:19.822
Whether it's somebody who's less fortunate than you,

2526
01:50:19.822 --> 01:50:20.790
or it doesn't even matter the form

2527
01:50:20.790 --> 01:50:22.450
in which the service takes.

2528
01:50:22.450 --> 01:50:24.170
It's the simple act of doing that,

2529
01:50:24.170 --> 01:50:27.760
that gets you out of yourself, and into somebody else.

2530
01:50:27.760 --> 01:50:29.620
And there's something magical about that.

2531
01:50:29.620 --> 01:50:31.710
That will shift not just your perspective,

2532
01:50:31.710 --> 01:50:33.960
it will shift your energy, it will shift your life.

2533
01:50:33.960 --> 01:50:36.840
And suddenly you start to forget about your problems

2534
01:50:36.840 --> 01:50:39.190
and there's a joy in that.

2535
01:50:39.190 --> 01:50:43.060
And you will always end up reaping more

2536
01:50:43.060 --> 01:50:45.250
than you are giving every time.

2537
01:50:45.250 --> 01:50:48.416
It's like this weird spiritual equation.

2538
01:50:48.416 --> 01:50:49.249
Yeah, and not only that,

2539
01:50:49.249 --> 01:50:51.370
there's science to back that up as well.

2540
01:50:51.370 --> 01:50:55.240
Because as we begin to practice,

2541
01:50:55.240 --> 01:50:57.640
again, express ourselves, animate,

2542
01:50:57.640 --> 01:50:59.520
do these different things.

2543
01:50:59.520 --> 01:51:04.520
We now start to engage and call on our nervous system

2544
01:51:05.670 --> 01:51:09.030
to fire off in new and different ways

2545
01:51:09.030 --> 01:51:14.030
and create new neural pathways that ingrain new behaviors

2546
01:51:15.550 --> 01:51:20.550
and new responses to external stimuli or to triggers.

2547
01:51:20.910 --> 01:51:24.720
So what used to trigger a certain behavioral pattern

2548
01:51:24.720 --> 01:51:28.320
now triggers a more empowered behavioral pattern.

2549
01:51:28.320 --> 01:51:31.170
And so all that starts to happen when again,

2550
01:51:31.170 --> 01:51:33.670
we allow ourselves to pour into others.

2551
01:51:33.670 --> 01:51:36.863
And again, we hear it in different language in business,

2552
01:51:37.832 --> 01:51:40.293
and Seth Godin's a big proponent of this,

2553
01:51:41.520 --> 01:51:43.580
when you start to deliver value,

2554
01:51:43.580 --> 01:51:46.810
when you start to give away your best stuff,

2555
01:51:46.810 --> 01:51:48.350
all of a sudden, what happens?

2556
01:51:48.350 --> 01:51:50.550
People start to see you as the trusted authority.

2557
01:51:50.550 --> 01:51:51.690
And pretty soon,

2558
01:51:51.690 --> 01:51:55.220
even though they could get the same stuff from someone else,

2559
01:51:55.220 --> 01:51:57.370
they choose to get it from you.

2560
01:51:57.370 --> 01:52:00.350
Well, in the process of you doing that you begin

2561
01:52:00.350 --> 01:52:03.870
to own being that trusted authority

2562
01:52:03.870 --> 01:52:08.560
and everything now starts to become second nature.

2563
01:52:08.560 --> 01:52:10.650
So what happens in business

2564
01:52:10.650 --> 01:52:14.930
also can happen in every context, in every area of our life.

2565
01:52:14.930 --> 01:52:16.220
Amazing.
Hope that makes sense.

2566
01:52:16.220 --> 01:52:17.420
No, it does, man.

2567
01:52:17.420 --> 01:52:18.980
I think that's a great place to start too.

2568
01:52:18.980 --> 01:52:19.813
How long?

2569
01:52:19.813 --> 01:52:20.850
Well, we've been going for two hours.

2570
01:52:20.850 --> 01:52:22.329
Oh, wow.

2571
01:52:22.329 --> 01:52:23.162
(Byron and Rich laugh out loud)

2572
01:52:23.162 --> 01:52:24.720
We gotta sew it up.

2573
01:52:24.720 --> 01:52:26.210
I think we did it, though.

2574
01:52:26.210 --> 01:52:27.250
Oh, this has been awesome.

2575
01:52:27.250 --> 01:52:28.883
This has been a lot of fun
How do you feel?

2576
01:52:28.883 --> 01:52:29.716
I feel good.

2577
01:52:29.716 --> 01:52:30.860
You wanna get anything off?

2578
01:52:30.860 --> 01:52:31.693
Well, you know what?

2579
01:52:31.693 --> 01:52:33.777
I feel like jumping on the bike and running.

2580
01:52:34.660 --> 01:52:35.493
I'm pumped right now.

2581
01:52:35.493 --> 01:52:37.160
Me too.
